    {
      "type": "prose",
      "caption": "Common confusion",
      "html": "<p>If the noun of the participle is already in the sentence, the participle simply agrees with it and there is no genitive absolute: ἐκβληθέντα ἐκ τῆς συναγωγῆς ἐδίδαξεν αὐτὸν ὁ κύριος, the Lord taught him after he had been cast out of the synagogue.</p>"
    },
